  "verdict": "YES -- the reconstruction-independent moment screen fires on GENUINE finite-sampling SQD undersampling at beyond-ED scale, DMRG-validated. At L=24 (sector C(24,12)^2=7.31e12, full ED impossible) the DMRG validator (E0=-7.6559, chi=159, trunc=1.0e-10) gives true weight M0=55.03; the SQD reconstruction from Born-rule sampling of the DMRG GS undersamples it by 95%->55% as the shot budget grows 500->15000 (|S|=495->13235), and the device-realizable screen Delta_0=|m_hat_0 - m_bar_0| (full sparse J,H on the SAMPLED |0_S>, no ED, no DMRG) flags exactly this: Delta_0 falls monotonically 43.5->24.5 (operator leak 94%->50%), tracking the DMRG-confirmed reconstruction error (corr>0.99). Same behavior at L=20 (sector 3.41e10). No false positive: Delta and the true error fall together as coverage grows; the independent estimator m_hat_0 (~46-49) stays near the DMRG truth while the reconstruction m_bar_0 is the branch that is wrong. HONEST SCOPE: 1D Hubbard is DMRG-solvable, so this is a beyond-ED CALIBRATION of the screen at the SQD pipeline's actual >ED regime, not beyond-all-classical; and at these budgets the current probe's weight is still 50-95% under-resolved, i.e. real SQD spectral reconstructions here are genuinely unreliable and the screen correctly says so."
